  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "DGET returns #VALUE! on zero matches, #NUM! on multiple matches, 0 for a blank matching cell, and rejects non-reference databases at entry (0x800A03EC)",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20527, DGET(database, field, criteria) returns the single matching record's field cell (returning 0 when that cell is blank), returns #VALUE! when no record matches, returns #NUM! when two or more records match, requires 2+ rows in both database and criteria, and rejects literal constants or arrays in database at formula entry (COM 0x800A03EC). All 5,668 full-bank DGET rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in CalcFunc-Evidence admit3-answers-dget-range-mixed.json, DnaCalc prefix_metadata row 267, and crates/calc-fml/tests/fixtures/entry/excel-entry.tsv; 5,668/5,668 full-bank rows match.",
